    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "American artist, geographer, and author (b. 1974); widely recognized for work on surveillance, AI, and photography. BA Religious Studies 1998 UC Berkeley, MFA 2002 Art Institute of Chicago, PhD Geography 2008 UC Berkeley. Runs his own studio (paglen.studio) with staff, represented by Pace Gallery (New York) and Jessica Silverman Gallery (San Francisco). Major solo shows at Smithsonian American Art Museum, Carnegie Museum, Fondazione Prada, Barbican, Vienna Secession. Awards: Deutsche Boerse Photography Prize 2016, MacArthur Fellow 2017, LG Guggenheim Award 2026. Sixth book published 2026 (How to See Like a Machine, Verso Books). Autonomy 5: independent artist at peak international career, fully self-directed practice, no employer above him.",
